course: dictionary
lesson: 9055
title: Sleepy and its two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word sleepy has two main meanings. It can mean tired and ready to sleep, as in «that evening he was sleepy and sick».
explain: It can also describe a place. A sleepy place is quiet, with not much happening, like «a sleepy village». To check which meaning fits, put your idea into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A tired boy is sleepy, but a quiet village is not tired, so the meaning changes.
explain: Context also gives clues about feelings. When the lions «lie flat in the shade like big sleepy cats», they are resting in the heat, so sleepy here means calm and relaxed, not unhappy or ill.
fact: Sleepy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a child, a bird or a village.
fact: «Sleepy» means tired and ready to sleep.
fact: A «sleepy village» is quiet, with not much happening.
fact: Yawning and heavy eyes are signs that you feel sleepy.
fact: Children who feel sleepy in class may need more sleep at night.
exercise: «That evening he was sleepy and sick.» What does sleepy mean here? | * Tired and ready to sleep | Hungry for dinner | Quiet, with not much happening | Wide awake and excited
exercise: What does sleepy mean in «a sleepy village»? | Very cold | Noisy and busy | Tired and yawning | * Quiet, with not much happening
exercise: Which word is the comparative form of sleepy, meaning more sleepy? | sleeping | * sleepier | sleepily | sleepiest
test: «The Rat feels sleepy and shut in.» What does sleepy suggest about how the Rat feels? | Excited about a new room | * Dozy and dull, with no fresh air | Hungry and cold | Full of energy and ready to race
test: «A bird sitting fluffed up and sleepy in the day may be ill.» Why might a sleepy bird be a warning sign? | It has just had a big meal | * It may be ill, so it needs to be checked | It wants to play with other birds | It is about to sing a loud song
exam: Which sentence uses sleepy to mean quiet, with not much happening? | My sleepy dog snored all night | I was so sleepy that I dropped my pencil | The sleepy lions were hunting at dusk | * The sleepy village had one shop and hardly any traffic
